1
00:00:15,711 --> 00:00:17,610
(With a light drizzle falling,)

2
00:00:17,611 --> 00:00:20,111
(it's early morning in Itaewon.)

3
00:00:21,151 --> 00:00:23,120
- Hello. - Hello.

4
00:00:23,121 --> 00:00:24,221
Kyoung Pyo.

5
00:00:24,681 --> 00:00:26,121
Today, you look...

6
00:00:26,721 --> 00:00:29,021
- gorgeous. - Gorgeous?

7
00:00:29,091 --> 00:00:31,020
- Is something wrong? - There's something...

8
00:00:31,021 --> 00:00:32,191
He lost weight.

9
00:00:32,491 --> 00:00:34,060
- Me? - It looks like you lost weight.

10
00:00:34,061 --> 00:00:36,161
- Really? - Yes, he lost some weight.

11
00:00:36,361 --> 00:00:38,731
- But I haven't changed. - Hello.

12
00:00:38,961 --> 00:00:40,331
- Hello, Eun I. - Hello.

13
00:00:41,031 --> 00:00:42,270
Has anything happened?

14
00:00:42,271 --> 00:00:43,441
Not much happened.

15
00:00:43,641 --> 00:00:45,140
- Are we getting something? - What?

16
00:00:45,141 --> 00:00:47,011
- Are we not getting anything? - I made an order.

17
00:00:47,541 --> 00:00:48,541
Thank you.

18
00:00:48,541 --> 00:00:49,541
- Thank you. - Thank you, sir.

19
00:00:49,542 --> 00:00:50,611
I got some Pu'erh tea.

20
00:00:51,441 --> 00:00:53,380
- I want some Pu'erh tea too. - Me too.

21
00:00:53,381 --> 00:00:54,381
Me too.

22
00:00:54,382 --> 00:00:55,680
- Pu'erh tea. - Pu'erh tea.

23
00:00:55,681 --> 00:00:57,821
- Pu'erh tea. - Pu'erh tea for everyone.

24
00:00:58,621 --> 00:01:00,050
- May I check your microphone? - Sure.

25
00:01:00,051 --> 00:01:01,091
(Checking BIBI's microphone)

26
00:01:01,291 --> 00:01:03,421
One of them fell off. I was fiddling with it.

27
00:01:04,921 --> 00:01:06,261
What are you wearing underneath?

28
00:01:06,731 --> 00:01:07,960
- Underneath? - I see.

29
00:01:07,961 --> 00:01:09,491
(There's another layer.)

30
00:01:09,831 --> 00:01:11,061
It's my underwear...

31
00:01:11,261 --> 00:01:12,361
Your underwear?

32
00:01:12,601 --> 00:01:14,430
- This... - You're wearing it on the outside?

33
00:01:14,431 --> 00:01:17,201
These are shorts I usually sleep in.

34
00:01:17,341 --> 00:01:18,970
But you wore them outside?

35
00:01:18,971 --> 00:01:20,640
- This morning, - You can have...

36
00:01:20,641 --> 00:01:21,910
I overslept.

37
00:01:21,911 --> 00:01:23,780
You can have that conversation in front of us?

38
00:01:23,781 --> 00:01:25,180
I didn't think they were underwear.

39
00:01:25,181 --> 00:01:26,750
I thought it was a fashion statement.

40
00:01:26,751 --> 00:01:28,310
When Hyeong Seo wears it, it looks like fashion.

41
00:01:28,311 --> 00:01:30,350
Send some to Eun I, will you?

42
00:01:30,351 --> 00:01:32,380
It's okay. She wears these shorts at home,

43
00:01:32,381 --> 00:01:33,390
and she's wearing them underneath.

44
00:01:33,391 --> 00:01:34,450
She was running late.

45
00:01:34,451 --> 00:01:36,150
I ran out of the house in a hurry.

46
00:01:36,151 --> 00:01:37,360
(During their underwear talk, the Pu'erh tea got fully steeped.)

47
00:01:37,361 --> 00:01:41,230
It looks like something came up with our guest today.

48
00:01:41,231 --> 00:01:42,231
What happened?

49
00:01:42,391 --> 00:01:44,200
The person who promised to join us had...

50
00:01:44,201 --> 00:01:46,161
- something come up. - I see.

51
00:01:46,501 --> 00:01:48,370
- It's nothing serious. - Then who's coming today?

52
00:01:48,371 --> 00:01:50,371
Are our friends coming?

53
00:01:50,941 --> 00:01:53,440
- I'll stand here. - Hello.

54
00:01:53,441 --> 00:01:54,471
Hello.

55
00:01:55,111 --> 00:01:56,911
I'm very grateful to one of them.

56
00:01:57,281 --> 00:01:58,710
He was invited on short notice...

57
00:01:58,711 --> 00:02:00,110
- around 10pm last night. - He was invited on short notice.

58
00:02:00,111 --> 00:02:01,981
- That short? - Yes.

59
00:02:02,811 --> 00:02:04,181
If there are two guests,

60
00:02:04,621 --> 00:02:07,090
let's guess who came at the last minute.

61
00:02:07,091 --> 00:02:08,491
Shall we guess who it was?

62
00:02:08,821 --> 00:02:10,990
(Who will be the two friends?)

63
00:02:10,991 --> 00:02:12,990
- Hello. - Gosh, hello.

64
00:02:12,991 --> 00:02:14,991
(Hello)

65
00:02:15,291 --> 00:02:17,030
(Everyone is happy to see them.)

66
00:02:17,031 --> 00:02:19,301
- Jung Ha Jun. - My gosh.

67
00:02:20,271 --> 00:02:21,530
(Today's guests, Ye Na and Jun Ha)

68
00:02:21,531 --> 00:02:22,830
- My goodness. - I see.

69
00:02:22,831 --> 00:02:24,800
I immediately guessed which one it was.

70
00:02:24,801 --> 00:02:26,610
- Jun Ha. - Hello, everyone.

71
00:02:26,611 --> 00:02:27,770
- Wipe off your sweat. - You're right.

72
00:02:27,771 --> 00:02:28,910
(Which one was invited yesterday?)

73
00:02:28,911 --> 00:02:30,011
My goodness.

74
00:02:30,341 --> 00:02:31,510
It's Ye Na.

75
00:02:31,511 --> 00:02:32,580
Have a seat.

76
00:02:32,581 --> 00:02:33,680
We called you at 10pm last night.

77
00:02:33,681 --> 00:02:35,011
- Thank you for coming. - Sure.

78
00:02:35,151 --> 00:02:36,821
- Have you been well, Jun Ha? - Of course.

79
00:02:37,281 --> 00:02:38,450
It's good to see you.

80
00:02:38,451 --> 00:02:39,920
I had no idea.

81
00:02:39,921 --> 00:02:41,420
- You had no idea? - No.

82
00:02:41,421 --> 00:02:42,590
- Really? - I had no idea at all.

83
00:02:42,591 --> 00:02:44,190
- Not at all? - No.

84
00:02:44,191 --> 00:02:45,191
Seriously?

85
00:02:45,192 --> 00:02:46,591
- It's Ye Na. - Hello.

86
00:02:46,891 --> 00:02:49,491
(Dancing automatically)

87
00:02:49,831 --> 00:02:52,461
(Everyone dances to "Catch Catch.")

88
00:02:53,901 --> 00:02:56,100
- Seriously. - Thank you.

89
00:02:56,101 --> 00:02:57,741
- We have Ye Na with us. - Have a seat.

90
00:02:58,101 --> 00:02:59,471
I'm sure that everyone can tell.

91
00:03:00,011 --> 00:03:01,970
Ye Na and Jun Ha aren't related at all.

92
00:03:01,971 --> 00:03:03,040
Of course not.

93
00:03:03,041 --> 00:03:05,080
- Between them... - But our names rhyme.

94
00:03:05,081 --> 00:03:06,580
That must be it.

95
00:03:06,581 --> 00:03:07,680
- "Ye Na and Jun Ha?" - He's right.

96
00:03:07,681 --> 00:03:09,880
- Ye Na and Jun Ha. - That makes sense.

97
00:03:09,881 --> 00:03:11,820
- Their names rhyme. - As I said earlier,

98
00:03:11,821 --> 00:03:15,250
we had invited Ye Na in advance.

99
00:03:15,251 --> 00:03:16,251
Right.

100
00:03:16,252 --> 00:03:19,091
- We called him at the last minute. - It was raining lightly,

101
00:03:19,591 --> 00:03:21,161
so I was having a drink.

102
00:03:21,331 --> 00:03:23,260
I had this gut feeling...

103
00:03:23,261 --> 00:03:25,400
that something was wrong when I got the call.

104
00:03:25,401 --> 00:03:27,030
At that hour, most people call you out for drinks.

105
00:03:27,031 --> 00:03:29,430
- The director called him. - Right.

106
00:03:29,431 --> 00:03:30,440
He asked me what I was doing tomorrow.

107
00:03:30,441 --> 00:03:31,941
Why is he asking all of a sudden?

108
00:03:32,641 --> 00:03:35,811
I had plans next evening.

109
00:03:36,011 --> 00:03:37,210
I said that I had work only in the evening.

110
00:03:37,211 --> 00:03:39,211
He said, "That's perfect."

111
00:03:39,441 --> 00:03:40,910
I didn't understand what was perfect.

112
00:03:40,911 --> 00:03:42,381
(I found the person I was looking for.)

113
00:03:42,481 --> 00:03:44,150
Thank you so much for inviting me.

114
00:03:44,151 --> 00:03:46,451
- Thank you very much. - It's my pleasure.

115
00:03:46,651 --> 00:03:48,550
Do you know BIBI well?

116
00:03:48,551 --> 00:03:50,360
- The two of you... - We're very close.

117
00:03:50,361 --> 00:03:52,520
She featured on my debut song.

118
00:03:52,521 --> 00:03:53,731
- Really? - Right.

119
00:03:54,691 --> 00:03:58,561
(They even performed together for Ye Na's debut.)

120
00:03:58,701 --> 00:04:01,670
We met through a variety show. We've spent time together...

121
00:04:01,671 --> 00:04:02,830
since then.

122
00:04:02,831 --> 00:04:04,770
We see each other often in private.

123
00:04:04,771 --> 00:04:05,900
- Really? - Yes.

124
00:04:05,901 --> 00:04:08,871
BIBI has a bold personality.

125
00:04:08,971 --> 00:04:11,740
I tend to think a lot,

126
00:04:11,741 --> 00:04:13,280
and I can't put things into action.

127
00:04:13,281 --> 00:04:14,710
- I hesitate a lot. - Let's go.

128
00:04:14,711 --> 00:04:16,720
- But she's a woman of action. - Let's do it.

129
00:04:16,721 --> 00:04:17,820
- She leads you to do it right away. - Right.

130
00:04:17,821 --> 00:04:20,720
- So we get along very well. - Yes.

131
00:04:20,721 --> 00:04:24,361
You get along really well, and you have great chemistry.

132
00:04:25,061 --> 00:04:28,491
But from her agency's point of view,

133
00:04:28,691 --> 00:04:30,260
- Right. - when Ye Na hangs out with BIBI...

134
00:04:30,261 --> 00:04:31,901
- Because I might influence her. - Exactly.

135
00:04:32,961 --> 00:04:35,700
(Because I might influence her...)

136
00:04:35,701 --> 00:04:37,970
- One thing is for sure. - She's the dark IU.

137
00:04:37,971 --> 00:04:39,070
That sounds a little harsh.

138
00:04:39,071 --> 00:04:40,371
That you'll influence her.

139
00:04:40,611 --> 00:04:42,440
Even my little sister's agency doesn't like it...

140
00:04:42,441 --> 00:04:44,180
when she hangs out with me.

141
00:04:44,181 --> 00:04:46,911
I can understand from the agency's point of view.

142
00:04:47,111 --> 00:04:49,851
Especially for idol singers, BIBI seems...

143
00:04:50,481 --> 00:04:51,750
(Upset)

144
00:04:51,751 --> 00:04:54,151
- Actually, I'm very wholesome. - Exactly.

145
00:04:54,321 --> 00:04:56,120
- When you get to know her, - I'm very wholesome.

146
00:04:56,121 --> 00:04:57,490
BIBI is actually not like that.

147
00:04:57,491 --> 00:04:58,521
- Right. - I agree.

148
00:04:59,121 --> 00:05:01,990
(Sweet and innocent)

149
00:05:01,991 --> 00:05:04,260
- But there's "gang" in it. - Most people think...

150
00:05:04,261 --> 00:05:06,161
- Gang. - Right, it's gang.

151
00:05:06,561 --> 00:05:08,730
There is nothing to worry about. BIBI is a good person...

152
00:05:08,731 --> 00:05:10,401
from what I've seen.

153
00:05:10,471 --> 00:05:12,140
(Did you hear that?)

154
00:05:12,141 --> 00:05:13,311
She is acting cute in front of the camera.

155
00:05:13,611 --> 00:05:16,170
- Please order something to drink. - Okay.

156
00:05:16,171 --> 00:05:17,911
Everyone is drinking something hot.

157
00:05:18,511 --> 00:05:21,481
- Please get them a drink. - One iced Americano, please.

158
00:05:22,111 --> 00:05:23,820
Both of you are in sync with me.

159
00:05:23,821 --> 00:05:25,250
- Both Eun I and Jun Ha. - Right.

160
00:05:25,251 --> 00:05:26,550
We've worked together for a long time.

161
00:05:26,551 --> 00:05:28,520
- We used to be at the same agency. - Right.

162
00:05:28,521 --> 00:05:29,751
We were in the same office.

163
00:05:29,821 --> 00:05:30,960
Since "Truth Game..."

164
00:05:30,961 --> 00:05:32,861
- that you hosted together, - "Truth Game."

165
00:05:32,991 --> 00:05:34,490
isn't this your first time on a show together?

166
00:05:34,491 --> 00:05:35,491
That's right.

167
00:05:35,492 --> 00:05:37,130
This show is quite similar.

168
00:05:37,131 --> 00:05:38,461
- To "Truth Game?" - Yes.

169
00:05:38,731 --> 00:05:40,000
This is a little different.

170
00:05:40,001 --> 00:05:41,001
(Teasing)

171
00:05:41,002 --> 00:05:43,340
That was filmed in a studio. We're filming outdoors this time.

172
00:05:43,341 --> 00:05:44,470
Right, it's different.

173
00:05:44,471 --> 00:05:46,101
- I guess it's different. - Do you know Kyoung Pyo well?

174
00:05:46,811 --> 00:05:48,670
- A long time ago, we... - We know each other.

175
00:05:48,671 --> 00:05:50,740
- We filmed a sitcom together. - That's right.

176
00:05:50,741 --> 00:05:52,880
To become a model on "Infinite Challenge,"

177
00:05:52,881 --> 00:05:54,250
- he had lost a lot of weight. - Right.

178
00:05:54,251 --> 00:05:55,251
He was extremely sensitive.

179
00:05:55,252 --> 00:05:56,680
When he played the bumpkin character?

180
00:05:56,681 --> 00:05:58,151
- The bumpkin character. - He was Jung Bumpkin.

181
00:05:58,421 --> 00:05:59,650
It was when he played Jung Bumpkin.

182
00:05:59,651 --> 00:06:01,391
Wasn't it when you got dust stuck in here?

183
00:06:02,121 --> 00:06:04,461
Jae Seok used to dust it off with a brush.

184
00:06:06,291 --> 00:06:07,531
- The lines were very deep. - Right.

185
00:06:07,631 --> 00:06:09,491
(Feeling nostalgic)

186
00:06:09,691 --> 00:06:10,831
Where are we going today?

187
00:06:11,031 --> 00:06:12,761
I don't know. They will tell us where to go.

188
00:06:13,061 --> 00:06:14,070
Is that so?

189
00:06:14,071 --> 00:06:15,670
- They'll tell us where to go. - I see.

190
00:06:15,671 --> 00:06:18,601
What is today's theme?

191
00:06:18,771 --> 00:06:20,241
Today's theme is...

192
00:06:20,471 --> 00:06:22,811
- "Why Can't You Order?" - What?

193
00:06:23,241 --> 00:06:24,841
"Why Can't You Order?" What do you mean?

194
00:06:25,281 --> 00:06:27,111
Everything must be in English because we're in Itaewon.

195
00:06:27,311 --> 00:06:28,380
What?

196
00:06:28,381 --> 00:06:30,221
Are we trying food from other countries?

197
00:06:30,521 --> 00:06:32,620
We might be eating something unusual or exotic.

198
00:06:32,621 --> 00:06:34,290
Maybe an international specialty.

199
00:06:34,291 --> 00:06:35,821
Or it could be an omakase.

200
00:06:36,091 --> 00:06:38,161
Forget about what you like.

201
00:06:38,321 --> 00:06:40,731
Eat whatever I give you. That's a possibility.

202
00:06:41,091 --> 00:06:42,460
Shall we take a look at it?

203
00:06:42,461 --> 00:06:43,560
(Why can't they order for themselves?)

204
00:06:43,561 --> 00:06:45,731
We will play this 1 by 1.

205
00:06:46,031 --> 00:06:47,471
I haven't seen it in a long time.

206
00:06:47,831 --> 00:06:49,631
- These will be clues. - I see.

207
00:06:49,831 --> 00:06:51,341
Please listen up.

208
00:06:52,401 --> 00:06:53,541
This is the first one.

209
00:06:55,171 --> 00:06:57,980
(First location: On-site reaction hint)

210
00:06:57,981 --> 00:07:00,281
(Swoosh)

211
00:07:01,251 --> 00:07:02,981
What? There's no end to it.

212
00:07:03,481 --> 00:07:05,350
- There's no end to what? - "What? There's no end to it."

213
00:07:05,351 --> 00:07:07,850
- The sound earlier... - Did you hear that swish sound?

214
00:07:07,851 --> 00:07:09,821
Wasn't it the sound of turning pages?

215
00:07:10,591 --> 00:07:13,930
(Tape 1, some kind of ordering system involving paper?)

216
00:07:13,931 --> 00:07:15,791
No, it was the sound of slurping noodles.

217
00:07:15,891 --> 00:07:17,400
Jun Ha, you know exactly what that sound is.

218
00:07:17,401 --> 00:07:19,161
It didn't sound like slurping noodles.

219
00:07:19,631 --> 00:07:21,701
(Pouting and sulking)

220
00:07:22,001 --> 00:07:23,371
- You made a mistake. - This is getting interesting.

221
00:07:23,641 --> 00:07:24,940
I should stay away from them.

222
00:07:24,941 --> 00:07:26,341
You're very pouty today.

223
00:07:26,741 --> 00:07:28,510
(Very happy, very pouty)

224
00:07:28,511 --> 00:07:31,180
We speak our minds freely to each other.

225
00:07:31,181 --> 00:07:32,340
I know.

226
00:07:32,341 --> 00:07:33,710
I've seen it very often.

227
00:07:33,711 --> 00:07:35,210
But it's been a while, so I'm happy to see it again.

228
00:07:35,211 --> 00:07:36,511
(Happy)

229
00:07:36,651 --> 00:07:38,081
This is the second one. Listen carefully.

230
00:07:38,951 --> 00:07:40,320
(Second location: On-site reaction hint)

231
00:07:40,321 --> 00:07:41,650
(Scribbling sounds?)

232
00:07:41,651 --> 00:07:43,721
- Is this right? - The resemblance is incredible.

233
00:07:43,961 --> 00:07:45,590
"Is this right? The resemblance is incredible."

234
00:07:45,591 --> 00:07:47,561
- It was a scratching sound. - It sounded like...

235
00:07:47,661 --> 00:07:50,090
- A drawing? - Maybe it's a pencil...

236
00:07:50,091 --> 00:07:51,930
- making that scratchy sound. - Right.

237
00:07:51,931 --> 00:07:53,331
It could be a shop where they do caricatures.

238
00:07:54,071 --> 00:07:56,970
(Tape 2, a shop related to caricatures?)

239
00:07:56,971 --> 00:07:58,201
The third and final one.

240
00:07:59,001 --> 00:08:00,140
(Third location: On-site reaction hint)

241
00:08:00,141 --> 00:08:01,240
(Tapping)

242
00:08:01,241 --> 00:08:02,711
(A sound of a machine?)

243
00:08:02,871 --> 00:08:04,541
What? Is it mind reading?

244
00:08:06,541 --> 00:08:08,350
It sounds like someone typing a message.

245
00:08:08,351 --> 00:08:10,281
- Right. - After typing a message...

246
00:08:10,851 --> 00:08:11,920
"Is it mind reading?"

247
00:08:11,921 --> 00:08:13,250
When something comes out with a whirring sound...

248
00:08:13,251 --> 00:08:14,421
"Is it mind reading?"

249
00:08:14,951 --> 00:08:15,951
What could it be?

250
00:08:15,952 --> 00:08:17,020
(They have no clue what the third place could be.)

251
00:08:17,021 --> 00:08:19,860
- This is just a feeling. - I like this kind of deduction.

252
00:08:19,861 --> 00:08:21,131
- What is it? - Feelings are good.

253
00:08:21,531 --> 00:08:23,761
- I think the first one is fake. - Why?

254
00:08:23,861 --> 00:08:25,060
- We haven't even started. - What?

255
00:08:25,061 --> 00:08:27,670
- The tone of the voice was... - Was it too...

256
00:08:27,671 --> 00:08:30,240
"What? There's no end to it."

257
00:08:30,241 --> 00:08:31,801
It sounded a little forced.

258
00:08:34,741 --> 00:08:36,741
Your close friend seems very disappointed.

259
00:08:37,511 --> 00:08:39,581
(- Ye Na... - BIBI.)

260
00:08:39,741 --> 00:08:41,680
- I don't think you caught it right. - "Catch Catch."

261
00:08:41,681 --> 00:08:42,980
("Catch Catch" is a big failure.)

262
