00:36:23,411 --> 00:36:25,141
- Is this what you ordered? - No.

1041
00:36:25,911 --> 00:36:28,010
I wanted beef brisket ramyun.

1042
00:36:28,011 --> 00:36:29,751
- But... - The beef brisket wasn't obvious.

1043
00:36:30,281 --> 00:36:34,020
I understood Song Eun I's drawing as a pork belly rice bowl.

1044
00:36:34,021 --> 00:36:35,691
(It became a pork belly rice bowl.)

1045
00:36:35,921 --> 00:36:37,420
For the brown meat in the drawing,

1046
00:36:37,421 --> 00:36:39,620
I used tare sauce, which is often used in...

1047
00:36:39,621 --> 00:36:41,421
Japanese rice bowls.

1048
00:36:42,131 --> 00:36:44,690
It'll add to the meat's smokiness and umami.

1049
00:36:44,691 --> 00:36:45,900
(Adding smokiness and umami by using a torch)

1050
00:36:45,901 --> 00:36:47,300
After placing thinly sliced onions,

1051
00:36:47,301 --> 00:36:50,571
it's finished off with a fried egg and chives.

1052
00:36:52,901 --> 00:36:54,900
But it still looks good.

1053
00:36:54,901 --> 00:36:56,471
- Spicy stir-fried pork rice bowl. - It does look good.

1054
00:36:56,911 --> 00:36:58,510
(Pork belly rice bowl is actually better.)

1055
00:36:58,511 --> 00:36:59,641
Score!

1056
00:36:59,911 --> 00:37:01,740
- I got something much better. - It was...

1057
00:37:01,741 --> 00:37:04,350
A surprise like that would be interesting.

1058
00:37:04,351 --> 00:37:05,381
Right?

1059
00:37:05,551 --> 00:37:07,280
- During the delivery... - It's here.

1060
00:37:07,281 --> 00:37:08,320
What is it?

1061
00:37:08,321 --> 00:37:09,950
- It's here. - What is it?

1062
00:37:09,951 --> 00:37:11,591
(The menu is served to Jae Seok.)

1063
00:37:11,961 --> 00:37:13,191
- What is it? - Carbonara...

1064
00:37:13,861 --> 00:37:15,090
It's Jae Seok's dish.

1065
00:37:15,091 --> 00:37:16,431
- Sir, I... - It's carbonara.

1066
00:37:17,861 --> 00:37:19,661
- Sir, I... - It's udon noodles with bacon.

1067
00:37:20,461 --> 00:37:22,370
(Sir...)

1068
00:37:22,371 --> 00:37:23,371
Wait.

1069
00:37:23,371 --> 00:37:24,371
(Running away)

1070
00:37:24,372 --> 00:37:26,241
(Jae Seok desperately calls for the owner, but...)

1071
00:37:26,571 --> 00:37:27,901
Don't run away.

1072
00:37:28,441 --> 00:37:29,710
Did he just leave after serving the food?

1073
00:37:29,711 --> 00:37:30,941
Isn't it too...

1074
00:37:31,671 --> 00:37:33,881
(How funny.)

1075
00:37:33,981 --> 00:37:35,511
It's too different.

1076
00:37:36,211 --> 00:37:38,281
What's more, I only eat oil-based pasta.

1077
00:37:40,381 --> 00:37:42,351
Anyone can tell it's instant noodles.

1078
00:37:42,521 --> 00:37:43,521
But...

1079
00:37:43,591 --> 00:37:46,321
(The spicy instant noodles Jae Seok truly wanted...)

1080
00:37:47,791 --> 00:37:49,790
The owner served something better than the drawing.

1081
00:37:49,791 --> 00:37:51,491
- I wanted to say that. - Right?

1082
00:37:51,961 --> 00:37:55,101
To bring out the color of the yellow noodles Yu Jae Seok drew,

1083
00:37:55,531 --> 00:37:57,230
I made a creamy udon...

1084
00:37:57,231 --> 00:37:59,101
with rich heavy cream and milk.

1085
00:37:59,771 --> 00:38:01,870
(Jae Seok's instant noodles order)

1086
00:38:01,871 --> 00:38:04,611
(Failed)

1087
00:38:05,171 --> 00:38:07,981
- What's this? - Udon isn't Jae Seok's favorite.

1088
00:38:08,781 --> 00:38:11,051
I kept mentioning it was instant noodles.

1089
00:38:11,851 --> 00:38:12,950
(This is hilarious.)

1090
00:38:12,951 --> 00:38:13,951
In your face.

1091
00:38:13,952 --> 00:38:15,790
Isn't this saying, "Get out?"

1092
00:38:15,791 --> 00:38:17,890
(Isn't this saying, "Get out?")

1093
00:38:17,891 --> 00:38:18,920
I'm shocked.

1094
00:38:18,921 --> 00:38:19,921
It's fun.

1095
00:38:19,922 --> 00:38:21,820
- Such a situation actually happens. - Right?

1096
00:38:21,821 --> 00:38:23,460
- It sure is funny. - It's really funny.

1097
00:38:23,461 --> 00:38:25,031
- Yes, it's funny. - Right?

1098
00:38:25,501 --> 00:38:28,631
(Either way, let's taste it.)

1099
00:38:28,971 --> 00:38:30,501
How is it? How's the taste?

1100
00:38:31,001 --> 00:38:32,141
It's still good.

1101
00:38:33,671 --> 00:38:35,200
(That's a relief.)

1102
00:38:35,201 --> 00:38:36,271
It's really...

1103
00:38:37,411 --> 00:38:38,541
It's delicious.

1104
00:38:39,641 --> 00:38:41,581
(Laughing)

1105
00:38:42,751 --> 00:38:44,150
- Pork cutlet? - Who ordered pork cutlet?

1106
00:38:44,151 --> 00:38:45,381
- Pork cutlet? - He cooked it based on the drawing.

1107
00:38:46,151 --> 00:38:48,650
(Nobody ordered pork cutlet.)

1108
00:38:48,651 --> 00:38:50,190
- Pork cutlet? - He cooked it based on the drawing.

1109
00:38:50,191 --> 00:38:52,290
- Oh, my gosh. - Is it Ye Na's?

1110
00:38:52,291 --> 00:38:53,391
- Amazing! - Pork cutlet.

1111
00:38:53,691 --> 00:38:54,820
- Oh, my gosh. - Is it Ye Na's?

1112
00:38:54,821 --> 00:38:56,690
(Serving it to Ye Na)

1113
00:38:56,691 --> 00:38:57,790
- Pork cutlet... - The color...

1114
00:38:57,791 --> 00:38:58,861
- topped with sweet potatoes. - Pork cutlet...

1115
00:38:59,461 --> 00:39:01,430
- It's topped with sweet potatoes. - It looks similar.

1116
00:39:01,431 --> 00:39:02,530
It's even better.

1117
00:39:02,531 --> 00:39:03,531
- Right? - Sir.

1118
00:39:03,532 --> 00:39:04,800
Ye Na, what did you draw?

1119
00:39:04,801 --> 00:39:06,670
It's a waffle with ice cream...

1120
00:39:06,671 --> 00:39:07,870
- on top. - That's a waffle.

1121
00:39:07,871 --> 00:39:09,171
A waffle.

1122
00:39:09,711 --> 00:39:11,811
(Ye Na's ice cream waffle...)

1123
00:39:13,181 --> 00:39:14,210
(turned into a jumbo pork cutlet.)

1124
00:39:14,211 --> 00:39:16,911
We interpreted Ye Na's drawing to be a pork cutlet.

1125
00:39:17,751 --> 00:39:19,581
On top of deep-fried pork cutlet,

1126
00:39:19,881 --> 00:39:23,851
deep-fried sweet potatoes were added to depict the circles on top.

1127
00:39:24,921 --> 00:39:27,661
(It's completely different from what she wanted.)

1128
00:39:28,021 --> 00:39:30,131
This looks good though. I like it.

1129
00:39:30,361 --> 00:39:31,461
- You like it? - Yes.

1130
00:39:32,331 --> 00:39:33,500
You end up eating more than you thought.

1131
00:39:33,501 --> 00:39:34,501
You're right.

1132
00:39:34,861 --> 00:39:35,971
I'll enjoy eating this.

1133
00:39:36,771 --> 00:39:39,741
(She quickly takes a bite.)

1134
00:39:40,241 --> 00:39:42,271
- Ye Na, is it delicious? - It's so good.

1135
00:39:43,471 --> 00:39:45,611
- Here it comes. - What's that?

1136
00:39:46,041 --> 00:39:48,410
- Here it comes. What is it? - I think that's mine.

1137
00:39:48,411 --> 00:39:50,381
- I think it's a wrong dish. - What is it?

1138
00:39:50,811 --> 00:39:52,380
It's bean sprouts dried pollack ramyeon.

1139
00:39:52,381 --> 00:39:54,220
- Bean sprouts and what? - Enjoy your food.

1140
00:39:54,221 --> 00:39:55,591
This isn't what I wanted.

1141
00:39:57,351 --> 00:39:59,220
- Bean sprouts... - There's clearly no brown thing...

1142
00:39:59,221 --> 00:40:00,861
- There's no meat here. - Was it on purpose?

1143
00:40:01,121 --> 00:40:02,230
(Kyoung Pyo's meat ramyeon...)

1144
00:40:02,231 --> 00:40:03,531
(Generous amount of brown meat)

1145
00:40:04,431 --> 00:40:05,830
- Dried pollack ramyeon. - Dried pollack ramyeon.

1146
00:40:05,831 --> 00:40:06,901
(It became bean sprouts dried pollack ramyeon.)

1147
00:40:07,101 --> 00:40:09,671
Out of all of ours, yours is the most similar to the drawing.

1148
00:40:10,001 --> 00:40:11,571
- That is true. - Yes.

1149
00:40:12,971 --> 00:40:17,041
(It still is ramyeon, after all.)

1150
00:40:17,941 --> 00:40:19,481
I don't enjoy seafood.

1151
00:40:19,641 --> 00:40:21,140
- You really don't? - No.

1152
00:40:21,141 --> 00:40:22,780
He put tons of shellfish. What a waste.

1153
00:40:22,781 --> 00:40:24,180
- You can't eat them? - I'll eat them.

1154
00:40:24,181 --> 00:40:25,550
Swap with mine, then. You can have mine...

1155
00:40:25,551 --> 00:40:27,081
- when mine is served. Swap. - Yes.

1156
00:40:28,121 --> 00:40:29,721
Shellfish smells incredible.

1157
00:40:31,421 --> 00:40:33,860
You're excited, Jun Ha. You'll eat with both hands.

1158
00:40:33,861 --> 00:40:34,960
(Slurping)

1159
00:40:34,961 --> 00:40:36,231
How does it taste?

1160
00:40:36,691 --> 00:40:37,861
It's so tasty.

1161
00:40:38,161 --> 00:40:39,830
- It's good, right? - This is crazy.

1162
00:40:39,831 --> 00:40:41,501
The food here is really good.

1163
00:40:41,661 --> 00:40:43,831
You could do this much, but...

1164
00:40:44,201 --> 00:40:45,601
they cooked like that.

1165
00:40:45,901 --> 00:40:48,870
An idea suddenly flashed in my mind.

1166
00:40:48,871 --> 00:40:50,211
- What is it? - It just came to me.

1167
00:40:50,541 --> 00:40:52,441
(Curious)

1168
00:40:52,611 --> 00:40:54,280
We all ordered the special menu,

1169
00:40:54,281 --> 00:40:55,981
but they're served very quickly.

1170
00:40:56,381 --> 00:40:58,480
What if the chefs...

1171
00:40:58,481 --> 00:41:00,550
from "Please Take Care of My Refrigerator..."

1172
00:41:00,551 --> 00:41:02,650
are doing the 15-minute cooking?

1173
00:41:02,651 --> 00:41:04,720
- They're doing it? - They're cooking really quickly,

1174
00:41:04,721 --> 00:41:07,821
- That could be the case. - and he just serves the food.

1175
00:41:08,191 --> 00:41:09,291
That could be the case.

1176
00:41:10,291 --> 00:41:13,101
Chef Kim Poong might suddenly appear.

1177
00:41:14,461 --> 00:41:16,101
Is Kim Poong really in there?

1178
00:41:16,731 --> 00:41:17,801
Poong?

1179
00:41:19,901 --> 00:41:21,301
I think yours is here.

1180
00:41:22,171 --> 00:41:23,171
- It's yours. - It's mine.

1181
00:41:23,171 --> 00:41:24,171
It's yours.

1182
00:41:24,172 --> 00:41:25,240
(Jun Ha's food is finally here.)

1183
00:41:25,241 --> 00:41:26,281
What is it?

1184
00:41:27,141 --> 00:41:29,411
- Ramyeon! - This is more to my taste.

1185
00:41:30,511 --> 00:41:32,080
- It's mine. - Ramyeon!

1186
00:41:32,081 --> 00:41:33,881
This is more to my taste.

1187
00:41:34,321 --> 00:41:35,851
- It looks like kimchi ramyeon. - Ramyeon...

1188
00:41:36,621 --> 00:41:39,160
- They made it correctly. - What is it?

1189
00:41:39,161 --> 00:41:40,791
- It's kimchi ramyeon. - Right?

1190
00:41:41,121 --> 00:41:43,531
- How is this kimchi? It's ham. - Just eat it.

1191
00:41:44,531 --> 00:41:45,961
- Sir. - Just...

1192
00:41:46,161 --> 00:41:47,560
(Jun Ha's ham ramyeon...)

1193
00:41:47,561 --> 00:41:48,931
(Two pieces of ham)

1194
00:41:49,731 --> 00:41:50,930
(It turned into kimchi ramyeon.)

1195
00:41:50,931 --> 00:41:52,840
For Jung Jun Ha's kimchi ramyeon,

1196
00:41:52,841 --> 00:41:55,671
I decided the rectangles he drew were kimchi.

1197
00:41:55,811 --> 00:41:57,471
I stir-fried it well in oil...

1198
00:41:58,211 --> 00:41:59,980
and made delicious kimchi ramyeon...

1199
00:41:59,981 --> 00:42:02,251
with curly noodles.

1200
00:42:03,481 --> 00:42:04,851
- Sir. - Just...

1201
00:42:05,581 --> 00:42:06,680
Just eat it.

1202
00:42:06,681 --> 00:42:08,951
Did you run out of ham? It says there...

1203
00:42:08,991 --> 00:42:10,891
I'm sorry, but you already had mine.

1204
00:42:11,051 --> 00:42:13,160
- You can swap. - I'll have this.

1205
00:42:13,161 --> 00:42:14,360
I'll have this.

1206
00:42:14,361 --> 00:42:15,830
(Jun Ha and Kyoung Pyo swap their dishes.)

1207
00:42:15,831 --> 00:42:16,831
This...

1208
00:42:16,832 --> 00:42:18,530
- This looks good. - This is delicious.

1209
00:42:18,531 --> 00:42:19,600
That looks tasty.

1210
00:42:19,601 --> 00:42:21,600
- Right? Would you like some? - Eat up.

1211
00:42:21,601 --> 00:42:24,331
(Kimchi ramyeon is really popular.)

1212
00:42:24,571 --> 00:42:27,101
- All that's left is BIBI's. - Yes, BIBI's.

1213
00:42:27,271 --> 00:42:29,041
- Here it is. - BIBI's.

1214
00:42:29,141 --> 00:42:31,541
It's exactly the same!

1215
00:42:31,771 --> 00:42:34,081
(Surprised)

1216
00:42:34,211 --> 00:42:35,751
This is what I wanted.

1217
00:42:36,381 --> 00:42:37,381
I did it!

1218
00:42:38,511 --> 00:42:39,780
(BIBI's menu is ice cream waffle.)

1219
00:42:39,781 --> 00:42:41,750
- I did it! - Was this what you wanted, Ye Na?

1220
00:42:41,751 --> 00:42:43,120
Exactly this.

1221
00:42:43,121 --> 00:42:44,821
(It's just like the drawing.)

1222
00:42:45,391 --> 00:42:47,120
The food is good here,

1223
00:42:47,121 --> 00:42:49,531
- but she mentioned Kim Poong. - Yes.

1224
00:42:50,131 --> 00:42:53,261
"Bunsik 85." Kian84.

1225
00:42:53,731 --> 00:42:54,931
He's close with Poong.

1226
00:42:55,771 --> 00:42:57,501
Kim Poong draws too.

1227
00:42:57,831 --> 00:42:59,471
Is there any word with "poong" in it?

1228
00:43:04,371 --> 00:43:05,411
"Landscape?"

1229
00:43:06,441 --> 00:43:07,441
"Landscape?"

1230
00:43:07,442 --> 00:43:09,811
(What caught Jae Seok's eye...)

1231
00:43:10,081 --> 00:43:13,551
(are the landscapes on the wall.)

1232
00:43:13,921 --> 00:43:16,291
(They're suspicious.)

1233
00:43:16,521 --> 00:43:18,051
Why are they hanging up those pictures there?

1234
00:43:18,921 --> 00:43:20,791
Is he really in there?

1235
00:43:21,291 --> 00:43:24,891
(Jae Seok's guess: The landscapes are hints to Kim Poong?)

1236
00:43:25,491 --> 00:43:26,631
But this...

1237
00:43:27,661 --> 00:43:29,601
This is a self-employed small restaurant.

1238
00:43:29,831 --> 00:43:31,301
Is this pricing really right?

1239
00:43:32,301 --> 00:43:33,741
Isn't ten dollars great?

1240
00:43:34,801 --> 00:43:37,511
If he does business like this, it won't last long.

1241
00:43:37,741 --> 00:43:39,981
The economy is struggling as is.

1242
00:43:40,611 --> 00:43:42,381
- Excuse me. - Yes?

1243
00:43:42,651 --> 00:43:44,411
Are you here to film "Baek Jong Won's Alley Restaurant?"

1244
00:43:45,681 --> 00:43:47,281
- You're giving them a solution. - Why do you keep...

1245
00:43:47,481 --> 00:43:49,190
providing solutions to all the restaurants?

1246
00:43:49,191 --> 00:43:51,321
I wasn't giving a solution. Look at the owner.

1247
00:43:52,121 --> 00:43:53,891
He's either a producer or an assistant director.

1248
00:43:54,391 --> 00:43:56,030
He must've come here in the midst of editing.

1249
00:43:56,031 --> 00:43:57,161
What's the director's name?

1250
00:43:57,691 --> 00:43:59,631
He looks like a Nam Cheol. Nam Cheol!

1251
00:44:01,201 --> 00:44:02,871
Kim Nam... Mr. Nam Cheol!

1252
00:44:03,601 --> 00:44:06,101
"Mr. Nam Cheol."

1253
00:44:06,571 --> 00:44:07,800
- Ye Na. - Yes?

1254
00:44:07,801 --> 00:44:09,470
It's been a few hours...

1255
00:44:09,471 --> 00:44:11,170
- since you've met Jun Ha. - Yes.

1256
00:44:11,171 --> 00:44:12,441
What kind of person do you think he is?

1257
00:44:14,141 --> 00:44:15,281
Be honest.

1258
00:44:16,751 --> 00:44:20,521
I think he'll have a carefree life.

1259
00:44:21,581 --> 00:44:23,751
(Laughing)

1260
00:44:26,691 --> 00:44:27,860
(Ye Na's innocent answer)

1261
00:44:27,861 --> 00:44:29,031
(Smiling)

1262
00:44:29,431 --> 00:44:30,661
I do have a carefree life.

1263
00:44:31,661 --> 00:44:33,101
Nothing uncomfortable.

1264
00:44:34,061 --> 00:44:36,770
You're like my dad.

1265
00:44:36,771 --> 00:44:39,440
- In what way? - Initially, he complained so much.

1266
00:44:39,441 --> 00:44:41,271
"Why do I need to do this?"

1267
00:44:41,441 --> 00:44:43,470
But when the food came out, he finished the whole thing.

1268
00:44:43,471 --> 00:44:44,510
You're right.

1269
00:44:44,511 --> 00:44:46,941
(Clean)

1270
00:44:47,081 --> 00:44:48,780
- "It's so good." - "My gosh."

1271
00:44:48,781 --> 00:44:50,480
- "How is it so good?" - "How is it so good?"

1272
00:44:50,481 --> 00:44:52,921
That's right.

1273
00:44:53,221 --> 00:44:54,781
- Shall we go? - Let's go.

1274
00:44:54,921 --> 00:44:56,591
Mr. Nam Cheol, we're off.

1275
00:44:57,221 --> 00:44:58,321
"Nam Cheol."

1276
00:44:59,461 --> 00:45:02,260
Anyway, out of the two,

1277
00:45:02,261 --> 00:45:03,490
that's the one.

1278
00:45:03,491 --> 00:45:05,901
The 200 dishes place was very suspicious,

1279
00:45:06,301 --> 00:45:09,901
but compared to the one just now, the first place is pretty okay.

1280
00:45:10,001 --> 00:45:11,731
When you consider...

1281
00:45:12,071 --> 00:45:13,840
the feasibility of the restaurant cost-wise,

1282
00:45:13,841 --> 00:45:15,641
with the turnover rate and so on,

1283
00:45:15,871 --> 00:45:18,341
- you can tell what's fake. - Yes, something like that.

1284
00:45:18,471 --> 00:45:20,440
And street food...

1285
00:45:20,441 --> 00:45:21,910
- needs high turnover rate. - Exactly.

1286
00:45:21,911 --> 00:45:23,580
- That's what street food is about. - That's the merit.

1287
00:45:23,581 --> 00:45:25,350
Drawing, scanning,

1288
00:45:25,351 --> 00:45:27,450
and waiting for the food took some time.

1289
00:45:27,451 --> 00:45:28,480
Right.

1290
00:45:28,481 --> 00:45:30,051
(The whole process took a long time.)

1291
00:45:31,221 --> 00:45:32,291
We...

1292
00:45:33,121 --> 00:45:34,890
We're looking for one fake place, right?

1293
00:45:34,891 --> 00:45:36,961
- Yes. - Are you finding the real place?

1294
00:45:37,691 --> 00:45:38,761
